{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/wc618f","slideIndex":0,"text":"Open with the central question: may lawyers collectively refuse to defend someone because of the accusation or public reaction? This presentation focuses on the Supreme Court's ethics ruling in the connected civil appeals in A.S. Mohammed Rafi v. State of Tamil Nadu. Source: Supreme Court judgment, https://indiankanoon.org/doc/153132263/; course journal case note."}
