{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/porqds3y","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":72,"top":168,"width":475,"height":58},"name":"left-lead","text":"The judgment dealt with two connected tracks.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":29,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#222222","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/mhkrehkb","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":72,"top":240,"width":486,"height":206},"name":"left-body","text":"Rafi’s criminal appeal arose from his FIR. Connected civil appeals addressed the Coimbatore Bar Association’s resolution not to represent accused policemen.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":25,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#111111","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/7it8nmlw","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":600,"top":170,"width":2,"height":390},"name":"divider","geometry":"rect","fillColor":"#D9D9D9","lineWidth":0}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/reh4jupc","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":660,"top":182,"width":500,"height":28},"name":"right-label","text":"THE ETHICS QUESTION","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":16,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#333333","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/6d8napor","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":660,"top":226,"width":490,"height":154},"name":"right-question","text":"Can a collective Bar resolution prevent every member from appearing for a particular accused?","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":34,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#111111","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/tgzml47i","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":660,"top":410,"width":120,"height":5},"name":"answer-rule","geometry":"rect","fillColor":"#555555","lineWidth":0}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/sfq5cz6x","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":660,"top":442,"width":490,"height":118},"name":"answer","text":"The Court said no. A collective boycott is incompatible with professional ethics and the right to legal representation.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":25,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#222222","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/xb3uv9","slideIndex":1,"text":"The judgment is a combined decision. The criminal appeal by A.S. Mohammed Rafi had its own disposition. The professional ethics declaration arose in connected civil appeals, after the Court noted that the Coimbatore Bar Association had resolved that no member would defend accused policemen in the criminal case against them. Source: Supreme Court judgment, paras 7–15, https://indiankanoon.org/doc/153132263/."}
