{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/fmho3i5w","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":696,"top":464,"width":460,"height":76},"name":"connected-text","text":"The observations against the Bar Association were quashed; the Court declared collective boycott resolutions null and void.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":19,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#333333","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/81scic","slideIndex":4,"text":"Separate the two results. In Criminal Appeal No. 2310 of 2010, the Supreme Court directed total compensation of Rs 1,50,000 (noting Rs 50,000 had already been paid), quashed FIR 2105 against Rafi, and quashed FIR 2106 against the police under Article 142. In connected Civil Appeals 10304–10308 of 2010, it quashed the High Court's observations against the Coimbatore Bar Association and made its broader declaration against boycott resolutions. Source: judgment, paras 7–10 and 12–34, https://indiankanoon.org/doc/153132263/."}
