{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/qpsb6dgj","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":102,"top":300,"width":1030,"height":32},"name":"item-head-0","text":"A fair trial needs counsel","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#111111","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/8b2xgr69","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":102,"top":338,"width":1030,"height":52},"name":"item-body-0","text":"The accused must be able to challenge the charge and test the prosecution case through legal process.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":19,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#333333","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/9wby9wne","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":72,"top":417,"width":6,"height":84},"name":"item-rule-1","geometry":"rect","fillColor":"#555555","lineWidth":0}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/m90feho3","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":102,"top":412,"width":1030,"height":32},"name":"item-head-1","text":"Public opinion is not adjudication","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#111111","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/na9g7m5o","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":102,"top":450,"width":1030,"height":52},"name":"item-body-1","text":"An accused cannot be denied a defence because the charge is unpopular or disturbing.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":19,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#333333","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/wz2xkrm5","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":72,"top":529,"width":6,"height":84},"name":"item-rule-2","geometry":"rect","fillColor":"#222222","lineWidth":0}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/x0bydwnq","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":102,"top":524,"width":1030,"height":32},"name":"item-head-2","text":"The Bar must remain independent","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#111111","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/axkfi1oz","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":102,"top":562,"width":1030,"height":52},"name":"item-body-2","text":"A collective resolution cannot make access to a lawyer depend on social approval.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":19,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#333333","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ubislu","slideIndex":5,"text":"A Bar Association cannot pass a resolution preventing all its members from defending a particular accused or category of accused. The lawyer's role is distinct from that of the judge: the lawyer supports lawful process, not social approval. The BCI Rule allows special circumstances for individual refusal; the Court rejects collective coercion. Source: judgment, paras 16, 30–33, https://indiankanoon.org/doc/153132263/."}
