{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/wfah4jap","slideIndex":6,"position":{"left":72,"top":170,"width":1136,"height":74},"name":"takeaway","text":"When the accused is unpopular, professional ethics matter most.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":38,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#222222","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/bihgzu90","slideIndex":6,"position":{"left":72,"top":286,"width":260,"height":32},"name":"practice-title","text":"In practice","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":19,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#333333","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/qx8fqpsf","slideIndex":6,"position":{"left":72,"top":334,"width":498,"height":150},"name":"practice","text":"Assess a brief independently. Do not let a collective boycott decide who may be represented. Preserve the court’s ability to test the case on evidence and law.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":25,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#111111","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/kbupsn6x","slideIndex":6,"position":{"left":640,"top":284,"width":2,"height":244},"name":"question-divider","geometry":"rect","fillColor":"#D9D9D9","lineWidth":0}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/lc3q1sni","slideIndex":6,"position":{"left":700,"top":286,"width":350,"height":32},"name":"discussion-title","text":"For discussion","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":19,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#333333","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/ypc7qdo7","slideIndex":6,"position":{"left":700,"top":334,"width":460,"height":150},"name":"discussion","text":"Can a lawyer personally decline a brief? How is that different from a Bar Association directing every member to refuse it?","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":27,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#111111","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
