{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/0lkdaf","slideIndex":6,"text":"Close with the distinction: the judgment rejects collective boycott resolutions; it does not erase the Rule's allowance for special circumstances in an individual advocate's decision. Ask whether personal refusal and collective coercion raise the same ethical concern. Citation: A.S. Mohammed Rafi v. State of Tamil Nadu, (2011) 1 SCC 688; AIR 2011 SC 308; decided 6 December 2010; Markandey Katju and Gyan Sudha Misra, JJ. Source: https://indiankanoon.org/doc/153132263/; course journal case note."}